 2. 📺 Trump cancels execution livestream 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Via Truth Social President Trump is calling off a livestream of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Hasan's execution by firing squad, Axios' Avery Lotz reports. 

 Trump wrote on Truth Social today: "I think streaming the execution for all to see might have been a strong deterrent for the World to witness how America deals with Terrorists and SCUM like Hasan but, many very good and well meaning people would rather not watch him die, through streaming, or through any other visual device." "That said, the execution may be viewed in person by the immediate families of the victims, if they so choose." 🪖 Hasan, a former U.S. Army officer, was convicted of killing 13 people in a 2009 mass shooting.

 Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said last week that Hasan's death would be livestreamed, drawing bipartisan condemnation. Chart: Alex Fitzpatrick/Axios. Data : ABC News/Washington Post/Ipsos 📊 The vast majority of Americans oppose livestreaming Hasan's execution, per an ABC News/Washington Post/Ipsos poll out this morning.

 80% of American adults said the execution should not be livestreamed. Opposition ran higher among Democrats (91% opposed) and independents (83%) . But even a majority of Republicans (64%) were against the idea. Go deeper . 

 
 
