 4. ☀️ 1 for the road: New sunscreen hits shelves 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios The first sunscreens using bemotrizinol — sometimes called BEMT — are hitting store shelves after the FDA approved them in June.

 Bemotrizinol has long been the go-to sunscreen option in Europe and elsewhere. Dermatologists say it offers broad protection but without the downsides of other sunscreens, including white streaking.

 BEMT has decades of safety data behind it, including studies showing that it has minimal absorption into the skin. Go deeper ... Learn more . 

 
 
